course: dictionary
lesson: 714
title: A word that names a job
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a person and what they do. Bargewoman is one of them. Look at its parts: barge and woman. A barge is a long, flat-bottomed boat that carries goods on canals and rivers. So a bargewoman is a woman who lives on or steers a barge.
explain: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad, dressed as a washerwoman, gets a lift from a large bargewoman with a horse-drawn barge. The clues are the boat and the horse: she is working on the water, not on land. A washerwoman washes clothes, so Toad's disguise is a washing job, but the bargewoman's job is steering a barge.
explain: Words for people can also be used to look down on someone. «I will not be laughed at by a bargewoman!» The words sound proud and rude, like the snobbish talk the word can be used in. Always ask: who is speaking, and do they sound kind or cross?
fact: A barge is a long, flat-bottomed boat that carries goods on canals and rivers.
fact: A bargewoman is a woman who lives on or steers a barge.
fact: In history, whole families lived and worked on barges on the canals.
fact: Longer words can be split into smaller parts to help you guess the meaning: bargewoman is barge plus woman.
fact: «Bargewoman» names a job, so it is a noun, and it can be used rudely.
exercise: «The bargewoman steered her long boat slowly along the canal.» What is a bargewoman? | *A woman who steers a barge | A girl who swims in the sea | A woman who sells cakes at the station | A horse with a long tail
exercise: Find and copy one word that names a boat in «a large bargewoman with a horse-drawn barge». | large | horse-drawn | bargewoman | *barge
exercise: Which two smaller words make up bargewoman? | bar and gower | barge and man | *barge and woman | boat and woman
test: Where did whole families live and work in the history of canals? | In underground caves | On steam trains | In tall castle towers | *On barges
test: In the sentence «I will not be laughed at by a bargewoman!», what tone do the words show? | Sleepy and calm | Lost and worried | Happy and playful | *Rude and snobbish
exam: A bargewoman steers a barge, so what kind of work does she do? | Baking bread in a village shop | *Working on a boat on canals or rivers | Flying aeroplanes over the sea | Mending roads with a shovel
